**4. Weakest Link Identification & Targeted Training**

After the examples above, the single most common weakest link at this stage is:

**“I understand the syntax, but I’m not yet crystal clear on the difference between interpolation and other bindings, and when change detection re-evaluates the expression.”**

**Feynman-style (to a 12-year-old):**

Imagine your component is the kitchen (where the real data lives). The template is a menu board in the restaurant. Interpolation (`{{ }}`) is like writing “Today’s special:
whatever is currently in the kitchen’s `product.name` pot” on the board. Every time the kitchen updates the pot (change detection), the waiter (Angular) quickly rewrites 
the board with the new value. You can’t change the kitchen from the menu board — the flow is only one way.

**Targeted training:**

- In your product card component, add both:
  ```html
  <!-- Interpolation -->
  <p>Name: {{ product.name }}</p>
  
  <!-- Property binding (different) -->
  <img [src]="product.imageUrl" alt="Product">
  
  <!-- Event binding (different) -->
  <button (click)="addToCart()">Add to Cart</button>
  ```
- Change the `product.name` value in code or via a button — observe only the interpolation updates automatically.
- Deliberately try something invalid inside `{{ }}` (e.g. `{{ product.name = 'New Name' }}` assignment) and see the build/template error.

Practice until you can instantly explain why interpolation is for *displaying text content* and not for setting properties or handling clicks.

