Direct prerequisites before deeper layers (e.g. property binding, change detection strategy, pipes):

- You can create a simple Angular component with a property and template.
- You understand basic TypeScript interfaces (like your `Product`).
- You know how to run `ng serve` and see live updates.

From your e-commerce project work, these are solid. If creating/editing components still feels shaky, pause and strengthen that first.

